.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_PKEY_DERIVE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_PKEY_derive_init ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_derive_init_ex ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer_ex ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_derive
.Nd derive public key algorithm shared secret
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_derive_init
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_derive_init_ex
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const OSSL_PARAM params[]"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer_ex
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *peer"
.Fa "int validate_peer"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *peer"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_derive
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "unsigned char *key"
.Fa "size_t *keylen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive_init
initializes a public key algorithm context
.Fa ctx
for shared secret derivation using the algorithm given when the context
was created using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_new 3
or variants thereof.
The algorithm is used to fetch a
.Sy EVP_KEYEXCH
method implicitly, see
.Xr provider 7
for more information about implicit fetches.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive_init_ex
is the same as
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive_init
but additionally sets the passed parameters
.Em params
on the context before returning.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer_ex
sets the peer key: this will normally be a public key.
The
.Fa validate_peer
will validate the public key if this value is non zero.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer
is similar to
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer_ex
with
.Fa validate_peer
set to 1.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive
derives a shared secret using
.Fa ctx .
If
.Fa key
is NULL then the maximum size of the output buffer is written to the
.Fa keylen
parameter.
If
.Fa key
is not NULL then before the call the
.Fa keylen
parameter should contain the length of the
.Fa key
buffer, if the call is successful the shared secret is written to
.Fa key
and the amount of data written to
.Fa keylen .
.Sh NOTES
After the call to
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive_init ,
algorithm specific control operations can be performed to set any
appropriate parameters for the operation.
.Pp
The function
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive
can be called more than once on the same context if several operations
are performed using the same parameters.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive_init
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive
return 1 for success and 0 or a negative value for failure.
In particular a return value of -2 indicates the operation is not
supported by the public key algorithm.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Derive shared secret (for example DH or EC keys):
.Bd -literal
 #include <openssl/evp.h>
 #include <openssl/rsa.h>

 EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx;
 ENGINE *eng;
 unsigned char *skey;
 size_t skeylen;
 EVP_PKEY *pkey, *peerkey;
 /* NB: assumes pkey, eng, peerkey have been already set up */

 ctx = EVP_PKEY_CTX_new(pkey, eng);
 if (!ctx)
     /* Error occurred */
 if (EVP_PKEY_derive_init(ctx) <= 0)
     /* Error */
 if (EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer(ctx, peerkey) <= 0)
     /* Error */

 /* Determine buffer length */
 if (EVP_PKEY_derive(ctx, NULL, &skeylen) <= 0)
     /* Error */

 skey = OPENSSL_malloc(skeylen);

 if (!skey)
     /* malloc failure */

 if (EVP_PKEY_derive(ctx, skey, &skeylen) <= 0)
     /* Error */

 /* Shared secret is skey bytes written to buffer skey */
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_new 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_encrypt 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_decrypt 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify_recover 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KEYEXCH_fetch 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive_init ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive
functions were originally added in OpenSSL 1.0.0.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive_init_ex
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer_ex
functions were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
